# Cutover Command Inventory

Legacy migration artifact. Not part of the current platform operator surface.

Use this inventory during controlled migration to `{{ platform_windows_wsl_distro }}`.

## New Platform Path

- Render Windows bootstrap:
  - `make render-windows-bootstrap`
- Verify platform host:
  - `make verify-platform-host`
- Capture pre-cutover evidence:
  - `make legacy-capture-cutover-evidence`
- Render cutover record:
  - `make legacy-render-cutover-record`

## Current Legacy Runtime Signals

Legacy runtime bind mounts:

- state mount source: `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_state_dir }}`
- workspace mount source: `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_workspace }}`

Current legacy Docker runtime:

- project: `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_project_name }}`
- service: `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_service_name }}`
- container: `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }}`
- image: `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_image }}`
- gateway port: `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_gateway_port }}`
- bridge port: `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_bridge_port }}`

## Controlled Stop Candidates

Review each command before execution.

- Stop legacy container `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }}`:
  - `docker stop {{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }}`
- Restore legacy container `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }}`:
  - `docker start {{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }}`
- Remove legacy container `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }}` after stable cutover only:
  - `docker rm -f {{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }}`

## New Path Activation

- Register the Windows scheduled task using:
  - `ansible/generated/openclaw-host-stack-windows-bootstrap.ps1`
- Start or restart the new host stack inside `{{ platform_windows_wsl_distro }}`:
  - `systemctl restart {{ openclaw_stack_target_name }}`
- Start or restart `k3s` inside `{{ platform_windows_wsl_distro }}`:
  - `systemctl restart k3s`

## Verification Commands

- `make verify-platform-host`
- `curl http://127.0.0.1:48721/healthz`
- `curl http://127.0.0.1:48722/healthz`
- `k3s kubectl get nodes`

## Rollback Commands

Use these only if cutover regresses service health.

- Restart legacy container `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }}`:
  - `docker start {{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }}`
- Restore the previous Windows task or launcher path
- Re-run post-restore health verification

## Operator Reminder

- stopping the old runtime is allowed only during controlled cutover
- removing the old runtime is allowed only after stable post-cutover verification
- record every stop/start/remove/restore action in `ansible/generated/cutover-record/cutover-record.md`
